As Ganesh Chaturthi approaches, conversations about home often become a little more personal. For many Pune families, the festive season brings a familiar question to the table: Is it finally time to move into a home that truly fits the way we live today? For those looking for a more spacious and thoughtfully planned home in East Pune, the Magarpatta–Mundhwa corridor is increasingly becoming a location worth considering.
Luxury homes in Pune near Magarpatta now offer a rare combination of established infrastructure, calmer streetscapes, and genuinely spacious 3BHK and 4BHK layouts, without asking buyers to trade connectivity for comfort.
Mundhwa sits in East Pune, Maharashtra, bordered by Magarpatta City on one side and the employment corridors of Hadapsar and Kharadi on the other. That geography matters more than it might first appear. A home here places daily life within reach of established retail, healthcare, and schooling, while still offering the quieter residential feel that many buyers moving from denser parts of Pune are actively seeking. Kumar World has spent more than six decades building homes across this city, and our own read on this stretch of Pune informs much of what follows.
Why the Magarpatta–Mundhwa Corridor Suits Premium Homebuyers
The Magarpatta-Mundhwa corridor works for premium homebuyers because it delivers short commutes, established social infrastructure, and proximity to Pune’s established premium neighbourhoods, all within one address. Families relocating from Pune’s older, congested pockets often find this combination hard to replicate elsewhere in the city at a comparable scale.
Living Close to Magarpatta City, Hadapsar, and Kharadi
Mundhwa borders Magarpatta City and sits within a short drive of both Hadapsar and Kharadi. For a homebuyer, that means daily needs, work commutes, and weekend outings rarely require crossing the length of Pune. Hadapsar’s established residential and commercial base, combined with Kharadi’s growing IT and retail presence, makes the area an attractive choice for homebuyers, gives Mundhwa residents two active neighbourhoods to draw on without living inside either one’s traffic density.
Workday Connectivity to Magarpatta IT Park and EON IT Park
Working professionals based in Magarpatta IT Park or EON IT Park benefit from Mundhwa’s position on the doorstep of both employment hubs. A shorter commute translates directly into more usable time at home each evening, something families with young children or ageing parents notice quickly. For entrepreneurs and consultants working across both parks in the same week, the corridor removes the need to choose a home closer to one employer at the expense of the other.
Everyday Access to Malls, Schools, and Healthcare
Amanora Mall, Seasons Mall, Phoenix Marketcity, and Inorbit Mall, which has been converted into commercial office and IT spaces, with the multiplex continuing to operate as PVR Inorbit Pune are all within comfortable reach from Mundhwa, covering everything from weekend shopping to family dining. Schooling options such as The Orbis School sit nearby, and healthcare access through Columbia Asia Hospital and Noble Hospital adds a layer of reassurance that matters to families with children or senior parents. This density of everyday infrastructure is part of what separates a mature corridor from a newly developing one.
Connections to Koregaon Park, Kalyani Nagar, Viman Nagar, and Pune Airport
Mundhwa also sits within reasonable driving distance of Koregaon Park, Kalyani Nagar, and Viman Nagar, three of Pune’s more established addresses. That proximity gives residents access to the city’s older social and dining scene without paying the premium those neighbourhoods command. Pune Airport (Pune International Airport) is a manageable drive away, a detail NRI buyers and frequent flyers weigh carefully, along with reasonable access to Hadapsar Railway Station, Pune Railway Station, and the Mumbai-Pune Expressway for longer trips.
